, "issue_field_values": [], "type": null, "active_lock_reason": null, "sub_issues_summary": {"total": 0, "completed": 0, "percent_completed": 0}, "issue_dependencies_summary": {"blocked_by": 0, "total_blocked_by": 0, "blocking": 0, "total_blocking": 0}, "body": "Hello,\r\n\r\nI have a question. I am using the Pixhawk Orange Cube Plus and MAVSDK to communicate between the Pixhawk and a Raspberry Pi. While I have successfully received GPS data, roll, pitch, yaw angles, and various other data, I have not been able to receive servo data. The following code is causing an error:\r\n\r\n```\r\nconst Telemetry::Result set_rate_actuator_output_result = telemetry.set_rate_actuator_output_status(1.0);\r\nif (set_rate_actuator_output_result != Telemetry::Result::Success)\r\n{\r\n    std::cerr << \"Setting rate failed: \" << set_rate_actuator_output_result << '\\n';\r\n    return 1;\r\n}\r\nThe error code is MAVLink: info: No ap_message for mavlink id (375) (system_impl.cpp:243), and when I connect the Pixhawk to Mission Planner and inspect the MAVLink messages, the list shows:\r\n\r\nVehicle 1\r\n L Comp 1 MAV_COMP_ID_AUTOPILOT1\r\n  L SERVO_OUTPUT_RAW (2.0 Hz, #36) 48Bps\r\n    L port 0 system.Byte\r\n    L servo1_raw 0 system.UInt16\r\n    ...\r\n    L time_usec x system.UInt32\r\n```\r\nAccording to the official documentation, the SERVO_OUTPUT_RAW ID has been replaced by ACTUATOR_OUTPUT_STATUS. Is it possible to modify the MAVSDK code to receive SERVO_OUTPUT_RAW? If not, are there any other solutions?\r\n\r\nThank you very much.\r\n\r\n![Screenshot_2](https://github.com/mavlink/MAVSDK/assets/114569363/84bd42a6-0480-4797-91dd-ca0a67d512c2)\r\n", "closed_by": {"login": "julianoes", "id": 1419688, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE0MTk2ODg=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1419688?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes", "html_url": "https://github.com/julianoes", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/julianoes/followers", 